text:
talia: Quick heads-up: i'm updating the model cards for nebula3b and vega13b to clarify per-variant max_sequence_length + add a short migration note for CLI v2->v3. PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-docs/pull/4521
noah: Nice. Any concrete numbers for the sequence ceilings? We should avoid saying a single global max.
priyanka: Runtime provided numbers: nebula3b(fp16)=6144, nebula3b-quant=4096, vega13b(fp16)=8192, vega13b-quant=6144. They asked us to prefix with "variant-dependent" and link to the catalog CSV for exact mapping.
talia: Perfect. i'll add a short appendix with the CSV link and a note: "ceiling may vary by GPU family and kernel selection". Also adding a tiny benchmark row for q4_0 vs fp16 at bsz 1/16.
omar: Small ask: please include a CLI migration snippet showing v2 alias -> v3 naming. A lot of customers still use the old `--model nebula3b-quant-lite` style aliases. We renamed that alias to `nebula3b:lite-quant-v1` in v3.
talia: Good call. i'll add both CLI and SDK v4 snippets. Keep them compact. Also will change model card key from `sequence_limit` -> `max_sequence_length` across the examples (we standardized that last release).
priyanka: Also fix the model-catalog table link in the card; it currently points to /models.csv (broken) — should be /data/model-catalog.csv. i'll paste the correct link in the PR comments.
docs-bot: Deploy preview up: https://deploy-preview.redwood-docs.io/pr-4521  (CI #11540) :rocket:
noah: Can we call out fallback mapping for quant aliases? e.g., `nebula3b-quant-lite` -> `nebula3b:lite-quant-v1` and note that the platform may fallback to `nebula3b-compat-q4_0` if the quant alias isn't available. That avoids confusion in runtime errors.
talia: i'll add a short line in compatibility notes: "If a requested variant is unavailable, the runtime will pick the closest compatible alias (e.g., compat-q4_0)."
omar: For the SDK snippet, use client.models.resolveVariant() so users can prefer quantized variants programmatically. tiny sample is fine.
priyanka: One more editorial nit: remove the inline HTML table for limits and generate it from the CSV so it stays in sync. I'll add a TODO comment in the PR for automation.
talia: ack. i'll convert the table to a generated include and add the CSV link. merging plan: small edits now, wait 24h for runtime final confirm, then merge. i'll keep the old alias references in a small compatibility paragraph for 2 weeks before removing.
docs-bot: Preview passed accessibility checks.
noah: LGTM overall. thanks for making the alias mapping explicit.
priyanka: pushed a tiny fix for the CSV link and the yaml key rename.
omar: added the CLI example. pasting-sdk snippet for quick eyeball:
```js
// SDK v4: resolve variant and generate with fallback
const variant = await client.models.resolveVariant('nebula3b', { preferQuantized: true });
let out;
try {
  out = await client.generate({ model: variant, input: prompt });
  console.log(out.text);
} catch (err) {
  // fallback to compat alias
  out = await client.generate({ model: 'nebula3b-compat-q4_0', input: prompt });
  console.log(out.text);
}
```
noah: snippet looks good. tiny nit: use `generated_text` field in the example payload to match the SDK shape in the docs.
talia: fixed. i'll merge the doc PR after runtime confirms the ceilings. thanks all!
